+A new method, ``set_error_reporter()``, was added to both the WSGI
+(:meth:`falcon.App.set_error_reporter`) and ASGI
+(:meth:`falcon.asgi.App.set_error_reporter`) application classes. It registers
+a callable that is notified of every exception raised while processing a
+request (including instances of :class:`~falcon.HTTPError` and
+:class:`~falcon.HTTPStatus`), which is useful for logging or for integrating
+with error tracking services. The reporter is called before the matching error
+handler, and it is also told whether the exception is handled, or whether it is
+going to be propagated to the application server.
