+.. _hookimpl_arg_default:
+
+Hookimpl argument defaults
+^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
+A *hookimpl* may also declare a default value for an argument. This is useful
+for a plugin that wants to use a new hook argument while still supporting older
+versions of the host program, whose *hookspec* does not have the argument yet.
+
+The value a *hookimpl* receives for such an argument is, in order of precedence:
+
+1. the value passed by the hook call,
+2. the *hookspec*'s default value,
+3. the *hookimpl*'s own default value.
+
+.. code-block:: python
+
+    @hookspec
+    def myhook(config, args):
+        pass
+
+
+    @hookimpl
+    def myhook(config, args, new_arg="impl default"):
+        print(new_arg)
+
+
+    # Old hookspec without new_arg: prints "impl default".
+    pm.hook.myhook(config=config, args=args)
+
+Once the *hookspec* gains ``new_arg`` (with or without a default), the
+*hookimpl* receives the value from the call or from the *hookspec* instead.
+This applies to plain *hookimpls* as well as to wrappers.
+
+.. versionchanged:: 1.7
+    A value passed by the hook call, or a *hookspec* default, now takes
+    precedence over a *hookimpl* default. Previously the *hookimpl* default
+    was always used.
 
 
